# Happy fork merge strategies. Rationale + the required one-time `merge=ours`
# driver setup are documented in docs/happy-patch-surface.md §7.

# pnpm-lock.yaml is tracked by BOTH upstream (slopus/happy) and this fork and
# conflicts on nearly every upstream import. On import (fork = "ours") we keep
# the fork lockfile and re-run `pnpm install`, so take-ours is correct.
# NOTE: requires `git config merge.ours.driver true` on the import host (see §7);
# without it this line is inert (falls back to a normal 3-way merge).
pnpm-lock.yaml merge=ours

# Committed build outputs. Upstream gitignores dist/ (tracks 0 dist files), so
# these do not actually conflict on an upstream import — this is a defensive
# belt-and-suspenders rule. The real issue is a gitignore-alignment
# inconsistency (these are tracked despite the root `dist/` ignore); untracking
# is a packaging change deliberately deferred out of M0. See §7.
packages/happy-wire/dist/** merge=ours
packages/happy-agent/dist/** merge=ours

# NOTE: `merge=union` is deliberately NOT applied to
# packages/happy-app/sources/text/** — the translation files are typed nested
# TS object modules, and a union merge that produces duplicate keys fails the
# type build (tsc TS1117). See docs/happy-patch-surface.md §7 (open question #4).

# NOTE: package.json (all packages) deliberately gets NO merge driver — it is a
# normal manual 3-way merge on import. `merge=union` produces invalid JSON
# (duplicate keys / spliced fragments); `merge=ours` would silently discard
# wanted upstream dep bumps; and field/dep REORDERING toward upstream is
# counterproductive (happy-cli US-001 proved re-sorting manufactures extra
# conflicts). Keep fork packaging + fork-only deps; take upstream dep bumps
# deliberately, one at a time. See docs/happy-patch-surface.md §7
# (package.json finding) + §4 (happy-cli manifest finding, Trap A/B).

# R8 sidebar trio (HA-10/11/12). These three upstream-canonical filenames exist
# in BOTH the fork and upstream but are ENTIRELY DIFFERENT features: the fork
# ships a collapsible e-ink sidebar + sidebar-restore control + avatar header,
# while upstream cli-1.1.10 ships a "new-session right sidebar" (2026-05-20
# design) + FilesSidebar. Operator decision #1 (2026-07-05) = KEEP the fork's
# versions as a merge=ours shim (do NOT adopt upstream's new-session sidebar on
# import). Requires `git config merge.ours.driver true` on the import host (§7);
# inert without it. `SidebarContext.tsx` is fork-only (no upstream equivalent =
# already zero-conflict, no rule needed). Upstream's FilesSidebar.tsx +
# utils/newSessionSidebarLayout.* would arrive as new files on import — adopt or
# skip deliberately (they are not conflicts).
packages/happy-app/sources/components/SidebarView.tsx merge=ours
packages/happy-app/sources/components/SidebarNavigator.tsx merge=ours
packages/happy-app/sources/components/ChatHeaderView.tsx merge=ours
